+On systemd platforms, upmpdcli will usually be started through a unit file. This is usually taken
+care of by the package. There is also an init file in the source tree.
+
+On FreeBSD, the Meson installation installs an rc.d script under the configured prefix,
+normally `/usr/local/etc/rc.d/upmpdcli`. Enable
+automatic startup with:
+
+----
+sysrc upmpdcli_enable=YES
+----
+
+The default rc.d script uses the installed `upmpdcli.conf`; set `upmpdcli_config` in rc.conf if your
+configuration file is elsewhere.
 
 
